Template: harmony-smp/reconfigure-notice
Type: note
Description: Reconfiguration notice
  Reconfiguration updates connection parameters and service settings.
  .
  Database: if you change connection parameters, ensure the target
  database is properly set up. The package will not create schemas
  or run migrations during reconfiguration.
  .
  Certificates: you will be given the option to rotate the signing
  and TLS certificates independently. Rotating a certificate backs
  up the current keystore and generates a new key pair.

Template: harmony-smp/rotate_signing_keystore
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Rotate the SMP signing certificate?
  The signing certificate is used to sign SMP service metadata
  responses.
  This will back up the current signing keystore and generate
  a new key pair. The truststore (partner certificates) is preserved.

Template: harmony-smp/rotate_tls_keystore
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Rotate the TLS certificate?
  This will back up the current TLS keystore and generate
  a new key pair and server certificate.

Template: harmony-smp/integratewithsml
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Integrate with SML zone?
  Enables SML/BDMSL integration for dynamic discovery.
  SML settings are stored in the database on first startup;
  the database is authoritative afterward.

Template: harmony-smp/smlurl
Type: string
Description: Full URL of SML server

Template: harmony-smp/smpurl
Type: string
Description: Full URL of this SMP server

Template: harmony-smp/smpip
Type: string
Description: IP address of this SMP server

Template: harmony-smp/adminuser
Type: string
Default: harmony
Description: Administrator username

Template: harmony-smp/adminpassword
Type: password
Description: Administrator initial password
  Leave blank to generate a random password.

Template: harmony-smp/serverdn
Type: string
Description: Server certificate distinguished name
  Used for both the TLS server certificate and the SMP signing
  certificate.
  Format: CN=hostname (e.g. CN=smp.example.com)

Template: harmony-smp/serversan
Type: string
Description: Server TLS certificate subject alternative name
  Additional hostnames or IPs that clients use to verify the
  server identity.
  Format: DNS:hostname (e.g. DNS:smp.example.com)

Template: harmony-smp/tomcatport
Type: string
Default: 8443
Description: Web server HTTPS port

Template: harmony-smp/database-host
Type: string
Default: localhost
Description: Database host
  Use localhost for a database running on this machine.

Template: harmony-smp/database-port
Type: string
Default: 3306
Description: Database port
  Must match database configuration.

Template: harmony-smp/database-schema
Type: string
Default: harmony_smp
Description: Database schema name
  When using a remote database, the schema must exist.

Template: harmony-smp/database-user
Type: string
Default: harmony_smp
Description: Database user name
  When using a remote database, the database user must exist
  and have rights to the "${db_schema}" database schema.

Template: harmony-smp/database-password
Type: password
Description: Database user password
  Leave blank to keep the existing password or to generate
  a random password during a fresh installation.
